            <ArticleTitle>Sexual maturation in Atlantic salmon induces a constitutive Mx protein production and influences the infectious pancreatic necrosis virus carrier-status.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-220</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1050-4648(17)30048-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fsi.2017.01.026</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this study was to demonstrate for the first time that sexual maturation induces a constitutive increase in Mx gene expression and protein production in Atlantic salmon. This could explain the reduction in IPNV prevalence previously observed in broodfish at the time of ova/milt stripping. For this purpose, Mx transcript and protein levels were analysed in different tissues/samples and compared between mature broodfish (female and male) and immature parr.</AbstractText>
